{"symbol":"MLST8","resolved":{"input":"MLST8","symbol":"MLST8","ncbi_gene_id":"64223","name":"MTOR associated protein MLST8","location":"16p13.3","aliases":["GBL","GbetaL","LST8","POP3","WAT1"],"uniprot":"Q9BVC4","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"MLST8 function (UniProt Q9BVC4, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): Subunit of both mTORC1 and mTORC2, which regulates cell growth and survival in response to nutrient and hormonal signals. mTORC1 is activated in response to growth factors or amino acids. In response to nutrients, mTORC1 is recruited to the lysosome membrane and promotes protein, lipid and nucleotide synthesis by phosphorylating several substrates, such as ribosomal protein S6 kinase (RPS6KB1 and RPS6KB2) and EIF4EBP1 (4E-BP1). In the same time, it inhibits catabolic pathways by phosphorylating the autophagy initiation components ULK1 and ATG13, as well as transcription factor TFEB, a master regulators of lysosomal biogenesis and autophagy. The mTORC1 complex is inhibited in response to ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q9BVC4","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q9BVC4/entry","title":"MLST8: Target of rapamycin complex subunit LST8"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12718876","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12718876/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:15268862","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15268862/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:15467718","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15467718/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:24403073","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24403073/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"MLST8 GO biological process annotations: positive regulation of TOR signaling, regulation of actin cytoskeleton organization, TORC1 signaling, TORC2 signaling","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q9BVC4","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q9BVC4/entry","title":"MLST8: Targe